Babet 2.9.x roadmap
====================

[x] Lot A: add configurable babet.spawn() redirections.
[x] Preserve the historical three-pipe default without breaking existing code.
[x] Add inherit, /dev/null, regular-file output and stderr-to-stdout merging.
[x] Add exhaustive validation, lifecycle compatibility tests and rich FR/EN/PDF documentation.
[x] Lot B: add binary-safe native babet.base64.encode()/decode().
[x] Lot C: add generic secure babet.writeFileAtomic().
[x] Lot D: harden worker lifecycle with strict options, status(), join(timeout)
    and cooperative cancellation.
[x] Lot E: add bounded direct worker-to-worker channels after lifecycle rules
    and shared transport primitives are stable.
[x] Perform the final code/tests/docs/PDF/build/release audit.

Babet 2.9.1 corrective release
------------------------------

[x] Fix chunked and connection-close HTTP response framing with cpp-httplib
    0.45.0 while preserving Babet-owned body/file limits.
[x] Add exact-boundary, fragmented, truncated, download-cleanup and
    close-delimited regression tests.
[x] Add independent blocking local smoke tests for both response receivers:
    HTTPS for chunked framing and HTTP for connection-close framing.

Babet 2.9.2 hardening release
-----------------------------

[x] Harden worker serialization with node and byte budgets, exact integer
    fidelity and exception-safe Lua boundaries.
[x] Harden spawn/exec/pipeline/spawnPipeline cleanup against C++ exceptions and
    post-fork allocation failures.
[x] Harden SQLite transaction recovery across callback, COMMIT and ROLLBACK
    failures, with reusable connection-state tests.
[x] Harden HTTP, socket and TLS exception boundaries and verify that
    Authorization is stripped on cross-origin redirects.
[x] Extend deterministic Zstandard, inotify, worker-budget and network
    regression coverage; validate the exact release tree under ASan + UBSan and
    the final normal build.

Babet 2.10.0 SQLite audit release
---------------------------------

[x] Audit every SQLite Lua entry point, native handle, bind contract and
    deferred-close path.
[x] Add the bind-only babet.sqlite.NULL sentinel without changing SQL NULL
    reads.
[x] Preserve useful step diagnostics after the parent connection userdata is
    collected and prove the zombie-connection regressions.
[x] Synchronise strict tests, French/English documentation and release
    metadata.

Babet 2.11.0 bounded archive-read release
-----------------------------------------

[x] Add babet.archive.read() for exact raw-name or one-based index selection.
[x] Refuse ambiguous names while allowing explicit duplicate disambiguation by
    index.
[x] Bound both announced and actually produced bytes with opts.max_size.
[x] Cover ZIP, plain/gzip/xz/bzip2/zstd TAR, raw names, workers, strict options,
    integrity errors and zero filesystem writes.
[x] Synchronise rich French/English documentation and release metadata.

Babet 2.12.0 SQLite connection conveniences
--------------------------------------------

[x] Add db:last_insert_rowid(), db:changes() and db:total_changes() with
    strict arity, closed-handle errors and 64-bit SQLite values.
[x] Add opts.readonly without changing the default READWRITE | CREATE mode.
[x] Add per-connection opts.foreign_keys with an explicit false default.
[x] Reject readonly=true with wal=true and cover all compatible combinations.
[x] Verify the new surface in the main Lua state and in workers.
[x] Cover ignored INSERT rowids and deferred foreign-key COMMIT failure.
[x] Apply the archive exception boundary to all public archive functions and
    verify TAR in-memory read completion explicitly.
[x] Synchronise rich French/English documentation and release metadata.

Babet 2.13.0 nested savepoint helper
------------------------------------

[x] Add db:savepoint(callback) with generated internal identifiers.
[x] Support standalone, managed-transaction, manual-transaction and nested
    savepoint scopes.
[x] Roll back callback failures with ROLLBACK TO followed by RELEASE.
[x] Clean up failed outermost RELEASE operations without forwarding callback
    results.
[x] Refuse db:close() while any savepoint callback is active.
[x] Cover strict arity, closed handles, nested recovery, deferred constraints,
    connection reuse and worker availability.
[x] Synchronise rich French/English documentation and release metadata.

Babet 2.14.0 remaining Lua/C++ exception boundaries
---------------------------------------------------

[x] Add one allocation-free exception-classification core shared by public
    Lua C function boundaries.
[x] Protect both compression functions and preserve atomic-output cleanup.
[x] Protect the six flat SYS functions without changing ordinary returns.
[x] Protect user.get and user.exists around their C++/NSS allocations.
[x] Protect the inotify factory and methods, with a non-throwing __gc wrapper.
[x] Add a compiled four-path self-test, verify reporting after catch cleanup,
    and reject all 17 direct registrations.
[x] Add PTY coverage for Ctrl+Z cleanup and terminal restoration after an
    is_running() status refresh.
[x] Document the current job-control boundary and the non-interactive pipeline
    contract in French and English.
[x] Synchronise French/English documentation and release metadata.

Babet 2.15.0 Lua longjmp / C++ RAII audit

[x] Inventory allocating Lua API calls made while binding-owned C++ RAII
    objects are alive.
[x] Audit local exception handling in socket, SQLite, archive and the remaining
    public modules before deciding whether any common-boundary migration is
    appropriate.
[x] Add focused tests before changing cleanup or boundary structure.
[x] Close the remaining process/pipeline registrations, structured userdata
    construction, and resource-owning finalizers identified by the final
    external audit.

Next planned release: 2.16.0 process terminal lifecycle and job-control audit.

[ ] Inventory stopped/continued child states and the consequences of adding
    WUNTRACED/WCONTINUED without changing the existing result contract blindly.
[ ] Decide whether Babet needs an explicit stopped/resume/foreground API or
    should continue to document bounded termination as its supported policy.
[ ] Investigate safe terminal reclamation when an interactive child exits
    before Lua next interrogates its process object, without doing Lua work or
    non-async-signal-safe cleanup in a SIGCHLD handler.
[ ] Add red tests for every accepted design before changing process state or
    terminal ownership code.
[ ] Keep pipeline()/spawnPipeline() non-interactive unless a separate audited
    terminal model is deliberately designed for them.

Deferred ideas retained in notes.md:
- parent-side PATH resolution followed by execve;
- forced worker termination (pthread_cancel remains intentionally excluded);
- macOS/BSD portability.
